From 5321c6fe357062a763a02b850328a7f504e12fbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derrick Tennant <derrick.tennant@automattic.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Mar 2026 00:26:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 03/19] feat: main-thread mouse click dispatch for control
 server
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

CLICK x y now dispatches SDL events from the main thread via
GFX_Events hook (before poll skip check). The click_requested
atomic flag is set by the control thread and checked by the
main loop.

Note: clicks dispatch correctly (OK returned) but SDL mouse
events don't translate to Windows mouse messages in DOSBox-X.
The SDL event injection bypasses DOSBox-X's own input pipeline.
Needs further investigation — may need to use the int33 mouse
driver interface instead of SDL events.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/gui/Makefile.am               |  3 +-
 src/gui/dosbox_control_server.cpp | 86 +++++++++++++++++++------------
 src/gui/sdlmain.cpp               | 19 ++++++-
 3 files changed, 74 insertions(+), 34 deletions(-)

